From 1de1c8055fe5fbcaf7a94f5fb7aff3b113d78b4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:46:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NotificationAttentionHelper: don't crash with favorites call
 lights on

The LineageNotificationLights constructor registers its settings
observer and runs the LedUpdater callback straight away, so
updateLightsLocked() runs before mLineageNotificationLights is
assigned. The favorites-incoming-call-lights block dereferences it
without the null check the rest of the method has, and with
com.android.server.notification.favorites_incoming_call_lights enabled
system_server crashes in NotificationManagerService.onStart on every
boot. Treat a missing LineageNotificationLights like "don't show lights
with the screen on".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../server/notification/NotificationAttentionHelper.java     | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationAttentionHelper.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationAttentionHelper.java
index 7b0206d1c..fba5fd0a4 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationAttentionHelper.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationAttentionHelper.java
@@ -1094,7 +1094,10 @@ public final class NotificationAttentionHelper {
 
         if (favoritesIncomingCallLights()) {
             if (!isCallLight(ledNotification) || mUserPresent || isInCall()) {
-                if (!mLineageNotificationLights.showLightsScreenOn()) {
+                // The LineageNotificationLights constructor calls back into
+                // updateLightsLocked() before mLineageNotificationLights is assigned.
+                if (mLineageNotificationLights == null
+                        || !mLineageNotificationLights.showLightsScreenOn()) {
                     stopPriorityNotificationLight();
                 }
             }
